# Committed on purpose — see the note in .gitignore.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the bundle by `next build`, and
# `npm run deploy` builds on this machine. Setting this as a Worker variable in
# the Cloudflare dashboard would do nothing.
#
# The prefix is the cache generation. Media filenames are not content hashed and
# every object is served immutable for a year, so whenever a re-ingest changes
# bytes that are already uploaded, the prefix gets bumped, the whole tree is
# uploaded there, and the site is deployed — otherwise anyone who already has
# the old file keeps it.
#
# v1 -> v2 on 2026-09-16: two case films were re-encoded back to the house CRF
# once media stopped shipping with the Worker and the 25 MiB per-file cap no
# longer applied.
# v2 -> v3 on 2026-09-16: client logos and video posters were re-encoded, which
# changes bytes at names that are already served immutable for a year.
# v3 -> v4 on 2026-09-18: the Hedin case split into two projects, and the five
# stills that had campaign copy burned across them were replaced by Alvin's
# clean re-edits — at the same filenames, which is exactly what the prefix
# exists to handle. Copied v3 to v4 server-side inside R2 rather than uploading
# 548 MB again; only the genuinely new files went over the wire.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MEDIA_BASE_URL=https://media.alcreatives.com/v4
